Schedule production with explicit precedence, capacities, and objective meaning (@mine-scheduling: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Operations-Research-in-Mine-Planning.lingua#r_3WX1KW34EWEGYZ6HGEMGGQBKHS", #source "../sources/MineLib-Benchmarks-and-Methods.lingua#r_3KXVJNVZ2FSQ8CZJMJG2JDQYR8", #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8") { r_1H23PH3C97H8PE2M8T9AYA0S7C
**Read:** [A Review of Operations Research in Mine Planning — Newman and colleagues](../sources/Operations-Research-in-Mine-Planning.lingua#r_3WX1KW34EWEGYZ6HGEMGGQBKHS), the complete planning/scheduling review and primary method selected; [MineLib — Espinoza, Goycoolea, Moreno, and Newman](../sources/MineLib-Benchmarks-and-Methods.lingua#r_3KXVJNVZ2FSQ8CZJMJG2JDQYR8), the complete selected formulation and data specification; [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the full planning/capacity context.

A production schedule allocates extraction, development, processing, handling, and other activities over time under constraints. Define period length, event timing, material supports, capacities, destinations, inventories, and objective before interpreting the result. A throughput total or value does not establish every necessary operating condition.

An objective can represent discounted contribution, recovered material, production target, or another stated measure. Net present value needs a consistent cash-flow timing/account and assumptions; benchmark or invented numbers are mathematical inputs, not current prices or investment advice. Physical and organizational feasibility remains separate.

Equipment, plant, access, development, ground, water, ventilation, blending, maintenance, and workforce can constrain different parts of the schedule. Aggregating them into one rate can hide the limiting process. A long-term plan may need shorter-term feasibility checks rather than direct execution.

**Work:** formulate a small schedule with named activities/blocks and independently check precedence and per-period balances. Compare a greedy immediate-value choice with an integrated schedule, explaining why they can differ. Identify a physically consequential omitted constraint and show how adding it changes the feasible set.

Read the complete review/benchmark specifications and relevant course planning material. Follow [Build a numerical validation argument across several kinds of evidence](../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8) for shared numerical-validation principles before the original exhaustively checkable example; the later project scales to complete primary methods and independently verified benchmark bounds.

**Continue:** [Build a numerical validation argument across several kinds of evidence](../../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/numerics/A-numerical-validation-study.lingua#r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8).

